  "html": "<hotgraphic-view modelid=\"63ae6b191422220804915691\" class=\"is-full\" sgpulse-type=\"component\"><template shadowroot=\"open\"><div class=\"component\"><div class=\"hotgraphic-inner component__inner\"><div data-socialgoodpulse-id=\"63ae6b191422220804915691\" class=\"component 63ae6b191422220804915691 is-complete\"><div class=\"component__header-container\"><div data-socialgoodpulse-id=\"63ae6b191422220804915691\" class=\"hotgraphic \"><base-view type=\"component\" lowercase_component=\"hotgraphic\" customclass=\"\"><template shadowroot=\"open\"><div class=\"component__header-wrapper  \"><div class=\"component__header hotgraphic__header\"><div class=\"component__header-inner hotgraphic__header-inner\"><div class=\"component__content\"><div tabindex=\"0\" class=\"component__body hotgraphic__body\"><div class=\"component__body-inner hotgraphic__body-inner\"><p>Cybercriminals use many different types of malicious software, or malware, to carry out attacks. Malware is any code that can be used to steal data, bypass access controls or cause harm to or compromise a system.</p><p><strong>Select the pin icons to find out more about three of the most common types of malware.</strong></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></template></base-view></div></div><div class=\"component__widget hotgraphic__widget is-tile \"><img class=\"hotgraphic__image\" aria-hidden=\"true\" src=\"./courses/ff9e491c-49be-4734-803e-a79e6e83dab1/470b0f8c-3433-58f8-8cae-ad9db92ba313/en-US/assets/63b6b477ce114563ba84d071581d4992.png\" aria-label=\"A wooden horse on wheels\"></img><div class=\"hotgraphic__pin-item-container\" role=\"list\"><div class=\"hotgraphic__pin-item\" role=\"listitem\"><button class=\"btn-icon hotgraphic__pin item-0 js-hotgraphic-item-click is-visited  hotgraphic-item-0\" aria-label=\"Viruses , Visited\" data-index=\"0\"><div class=\"hotgraphic__pin-icon hotgraphic-check_circle \"><material-icon icon=\"check\" class=\"hotgraphic-btn-icon\" customclasses=\"\" iconname